----------
scriptunit-fragment 1
----------

var b = 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment 2
----------

let n = 3

----------
scriptunit-fragment 3
----------

var i = 0
loop while i .< n
  set b = b * 2
  set i = i + 1
end loop

----------
scriptunit-fragment 4
----------

let c = b + 1

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 8 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `n` = 3 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1), reads `n` (2) | compiles, runs | new | `i` = 3 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 9 |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

let n = 4

----------
expect unit 2 is edited to loop once more
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | reruns | rerun: unit 3 updates `b` when it last ran, and reruns | `b` = 16 |
| 2 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | `n` = 4 |
| 3 | updates `b` (1), reads `n` (2) | reruns | reads `n` from unit 2 | `i` = 4 |
| 4 | reads `b` (1) | reruns | reads `b` after unit 3, which wrote a new value | `c` = 17 |

